\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\i (Very experimental \u8212- you probably want {\f1 --side-bias} instead.)} Scales the precision of MS bands globally (both mid and side together), LAME {\f1 -q} style. 256=no change, 384~1.5x, 512~2x. In practice its reach is limited: above ~600-800 the threshold hits FDK's hard floor and under CBR bits are only shifted between bands, so the sound stops changing. Superseded for stereo tuning by {\f1 --side-bias}/{\f1 --side-knee}, which act per-channel exactly where it matters.\par}
\cell}
