\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --mid-bias <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 256..no limit (Q8)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (off)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\i (Very experimental \u8212- rarely needed.)} {\f1 >256} RAISES the mid (L+R) threshold after the MS butterfly to free bits from mid for side. The cleaner, better-measured way to shift the mid\u8596 ?side balance is {\f1 --side-bias} (which pulls from the same budget from the side end). Kept for completeness. 256=off.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --side-bias <dB>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -24.0 .. +50.0\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 0 (off)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b The main stereo-quality knob.} Shifts the SIDE (L\u8722 ?R) channel's masking threshold on MS-coded bands, at the exact point where FDK decides whether a scalefactor band is coded or dropped ({\f1 energy > threshold} in {\f1 sf_estim.cpp}). Sign = EFFECT: {\b {\f1 +} steers MORE bits to the side channel} (lower threshold \u8594 ? fewer side bands zeroed, the survivors quantized finer \u8594 ? cleaner stereo width, reverb tails, ambience), at the mid channel's expense; {\b {\f1 \u8722 ?} deliberately DEGRADES the side} (raises the threshold \u8594 ? side bands drop out \u8594 ? narrower, more mono image). This is the very same energy-vs-threshold decision LAME rides for its bit allocation and MusePack drives with {\f1 --ms} \u8212- nothing exotic. Because it is a fixed-budget tradeoff, at low bitrate the mid channel audibly gives up bits; that is expected, not a bug. Sane range {\b +3 .. +9} for "more spacious", negative only for extreme/artistic low-bitrate mangling. Measured on real material at 96 kbps: {\f1 +9} lifts side error in the 4\u8211-8 kHz region while mid degrades a few dB. 0 = off (bit-identical to stock).\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --side-knee <dB>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -24.0 .. +50.0\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 0 (off)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Shapes HOW SHARPLY a side band flips between "coded" and "zeroed" at the threshold. Stock FDK is a hard cliff: the instant {\f1 energy \u8804 ? threshold} the whole band is dropped to zero. {\b {\f1 +} = SOFT knee}: bands sitting up to N dB {\i below} the threshold are still kept (coded at the coarsest scalefactor) instead of dropped, so the side fades out gradually rather than switching off \u8212- smoother decay of reverb/air. {\b {\f1 \u8722 ?} = HARD knee}: bands that only just clear the threshold (within N dB {\i above} it) are forced to zero anyway, cutting the side off early \u8212- leaner, more aggressive. Ortogonal to {\f1 --side-bias} and combines with it. Sane range {\b +3 .. +6}. 0 = off.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --mask-slope <dB>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -24.0 .. +50.0\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 0 (off)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Global (mid {\b and} side) tuning of FDK's {\b Masking-Slope-Adaptation} \u8212- a NON-masking heuristic ({\f1 adj_thr.cpp}) that relaxes the required SNR for scalefactor bands whose energy sits far below the frame average (stock: more than ~10 dB below), i.e. it deliberately starves very quiet bands to save bits. This knob shifts that "how far below average before I stop caring" threshold. {\b {\f1 +} raises it \u8594 ? fewer quiet bands starved \u8594 ? more detail in quiet passages, reverb tails, decays} (costs bits); {\b {\f1 \u8722 ?} lowers it \u8594 ? quiet bands starved harder \u8594 ? leaner, hollower, more bits for the loud stuff}. Same family as {\f1 --side-bias} but applied to both channels and keyed on energy-vs-average rather than the MS threshold. Subtle on dense material (it only touches the quietest bands); most audible on sparse/reverberant content. Sane range {\b \u177 ?6 .. \u177 ?12}. 0 = off.\par}
\cell}
}
