{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Example (your case \u8212- 7.5 kHz of core at HE-AAC v2 48 kbps, where the table gives less):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 fdkaac-franken-x64.exe -p 29 -b 48000 --core-cutoff 7500 -o out.m4a in.wav\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Verified: {\f1 --core-cutoff 7500} -> effective bandwidth 7500 Hz; stock {\f1 -w 7500} under SBR stays 8613 Hz (ignored).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NOTE: you police the core limits yourself. The max is the core Nyquist ({\f1 sr/2}), and with {\b dual-rate SBR the target samplerate is divided by 2} \u8212- keep that in mind when choosing values.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 3. Density / precision of SBR data\par}
