\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 SBR noise floor offset (small integer). Larger = more filling noise in the SBR reconstruction.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --sbr-header-period <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 off, >=1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Frames between SBR headers = how fast the SBR high band "kicks in" when a decoder tunes into a live HE-AAC stream (Icecast/Shoutcast). The SBR CONFIG lives in a periodic header, not in every frame; a decoder joining mid-stream plays core-only (muffled) until the next header arrives. {\f1 1} = header in every frame \u8594 ? near-instant SBR lock (~23 ms); higher = longer core-only moment. FDK default is ~10 frames (~0.23 s HE dual-rate / ~0.46 s LC). FDK caps this to at most once per second, so very large values are clamped (e.g. 40 \u8594 ? 21 frames @44.1k). See {\f1 --verbose} for the effective period in ms.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --sbr-noise-max <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 6, 3, -3\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (tuning table)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Ceiling on how loud the noise SBR injects into the high band may get: {\f1 6} = 1.0, {\f1 3} = 0.5, {\f1 -3} = 0.125. This is the "air versus hiss" limit. Already a config field inside FDK, just never reachable from the command line.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --sbr-tran-peak <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 1..200\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (90 = 0.90)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Transient detector: how {\i peaky} an attack must be. A slot counts as a transient only once the signal falls below this fraction of the previous slot. Raw x100, so {\f1 90} is the stock 0.90. Higher = fewer transients detected.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --sbr-tran-thr <n>}\par}
\cell}
