{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NOTE on units: knobs documented as {\f1 x100} are multipliers on a stock constant, where {\f1 100} means 1.00 and is an exact no-op. Knobs documented as {\i raw} x100 replace the constant outright ({\f1 --sbr-tran-peak 90} {\b is} the stock 0.90). {\f1 --sbr-mh-maxcomp} and {\f1 --sbr-mh-deltatime} are plain integers, and {\f1 --sbr-noise-max} takes only the three values FDK's noise estimator understands.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MEASURED - pre-echo in the SBR band. This is the one result worth acting on. Test signal: 24 percussive attacks (hi-hat/clap character) plus four decaying tones between 8 and 13 kHz. Metric: energy above 9 kHz appearing in the two 5.8 ms windows {\i before} each attack that is not present in the source - i.e. audible smearing of the attack backwards in time. Encoded as HE-AAC, decoded with ffmpeg, lag-aligned by cross-correlation first:\par}
