{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Switch\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Values\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Default\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Description\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ps <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 auto, 0 off, 1 on\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Force sending the PS IID parameter. {\f1 0} = never (flattens the stereo image), {\f1 1} = always. Overrides the loudness-difference heuristic.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ps-iid-quant <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 def, 0 coarse, 1 fine\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 IID quantization grid: coarse vs. fine.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ps-icc <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 auto, 0 off, 1 on\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Force ICC (Interchannel Coherence \u8212- channel similarity/coherence) on/off.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ps-icc-mode <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 def, 0/1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 ICC rotation mode: 0 = ROT_A, 1 = ROT_B. Signalling only \u8212- the same matrix, derived differently by the decoder, so treat this as a compatibility knob rather than a quality one.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ps-bands <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 10 or 20\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (bitrate table)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Number of PS stereo bands = {\b frequency} resolution of the stereo parameters. Stock FDK derives this from the bitrate alone, so at 22 kbps and above you always get 20 and can never audition 10. Fewer bands = coarser stereo image, fewer parameter bits.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ps-env <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 1, 2 or 4\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (bitrate table)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 PS parameter envelopes per frame = {\b time} resolution of the stereo parameters. Above 36 kbps stock FDK always picks 4. More envelopes track a moving panorama and transients more closely.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ps-env-reduce <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 0, 1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (on)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 0} disables the automatic envelope-halving loop ({\f1 envelopeReducible}). By default FDK keeps collapsing 4 envelopes to 2 to 1 whenever neighbouring envelopes look similar by a hardcoded error threshold, so the envelope count you configured is often {\i not} what gets transmitted. {\f1 0} makes {\f1 --ps-env} literal.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --ps-noenv-skip <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 0, 1\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (on)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 0} forbids parameter-less PS frames. By default FDK may emit up to 10 consecutive frames carrying {\b no} stereo parameters at all when successive IID/ICC sets look similar, which can be heard as the stereo image briefly collapsing and snapping back. {\f1 0} = always send parameters.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NOTE about PS resolution: {\f1 --ps-bands} and {\f1 --ps-env} are the two axes that change {\i how many} stereo parameters are actually transmitted \u8212- in frequency and in time respectively. That makes them considerably more audible than {\f1 --ps-icc-mode}, which only changes how the same matrix is signalled. Measured on a 4-second stereo probe with a deliberately moving panorama (0.25 Hz) plus alternating L/R transients, encoded as HE-AAC v2 at 48 kbps, comparing the panorama trajectory of the decoded file against the source:\par}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
