\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Default\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Description\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --vbr-reservoir <bits>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 0..(6144*channels - average)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (off)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Bit-reservoir size. More = wider frame spread around the average. min 0 (stick to the target tightly). Auto-clamped to the ceiling - you can't overdo it. Safe start: 2-3x default.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --peak-bitrate <bps>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 > target\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (off)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Allows short peaks up to this value while keeping the average. Set ABOVE {\f1 -b} (e.g. -b 128000 --peak-bitrate 160000). Below the target it is ignored.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --max-bits-frame <bits>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 average..12288(st.)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (off)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Hard ceiling of bits in ONE frame. Must be >= average and <= 6144*channels (otherwise clamped). Reasonable cap ~1.5x average (~4500 for 128k st.). Too low = starves loud frames (audible).\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --min-bits-frame <bits>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 0..average\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (off)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Hard floor of bits/frame. A higher floor wastes bits on silence. Leave at 0 unless experimenting.\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{
\trowd \trgaph120
\cellx2160\cellx4320\cellx6480\cellx8640
\trkeep\intbl
{
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\f1 --bitres-mode <n>}\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 0/1/2\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 -1 (def)\par}
\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Reservoir mode: 0 full (like default), 1 reduced, 2 disabled (rigid, closest to hard per-frame CBR).\par}
\cell}
}
\intbl\row}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 HOW TO SET IT OPTIMALLY (for the less experienced - so you don't overdo it):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Safe quasi-CVBR ~128k stereo: {\f1 -b 128000 --peak-bitrate 160000 --vbr-reservoir 6000}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Do NOT set {\f1 --max-bits-frame} BELOW the average or {\f1 --min-bits-frame} ABOVE the average - that fights the target and ruins quality.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 --vbr-reservoir} is auto-clamped to the ceiling, so it's safe to experiment.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Measured for real (4s variable signal, 128k stereo): CBR default spread 95-167 kbps; with {\f1 --vbr-reservoir 8000 --peak-bitrate 192000} spread 36-158 kbps (breathes harder, average held); {\f1 --bitres-mode 2} spread 127.8-128.2 (rigid). All fully decodable.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Limitation: this is a CBR+reservoir engine, not true ABR like LAME. Swings are moderate (6144 bits/channel limit), but this is that "light flight" of AAC.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 10. Audiophile / extreme (opt-in, beyond the typical range)\par}
