\intbl\row}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 How much it saves (2 s, 128k stereo, measured): default ~34381 B \u8594 ? {\f1 --no-tool-tag} ~34297 B (\u8722 ?84) \u8594 ? {\f1 --minimal-moov} ~34048 B (\u8722 ?333). These are small numbers \u8212- the MP4 overhead is mostly the mandatory skeleton, which can't be removed. Want truly zero container overhead? Use raw ADTS: {\f1 -f 2 -o out.aac} (a stream without any boxes, but also without tags and gapless).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 NOTE on gapless: {\f1 --minimal-moov} removes iTunSMPB, so when joining tracks micro-gaps may appear (the encoder delay won't be signaled). For ordinary listening this doesn't matter; for "gapless" albums leave the defaults.\par}
